--     84 picker services (16 NEW, Tea ceremony master corrected to its own
--     service), every specialty value scoped by event, and live_key_map
--     placing each of the 296 live keys exactly once.
--   · supabase/data/taxonomy-merge-2026-11-06.json — the approved merge map,
--     used only for what v2 does not restate: which category a key sits in
--     today and where each folded category goes.
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES (one transaction — the DO block):
--   1. Refuses to run unless both merge mechanisms exist.
--   2. Creates the two NEW categories (Staff, security & registration ·
--      Prayers & novena) under their group's folder.
--   3. Creates the 16 NEW services (canonical_service_taxonomy + schema row).
--   4. Re-tiles every live key and every v2 service onto its v2 category.
--   5. Merges each folded category into its destination
--      (merge_service_category — couples' suppliers on running events move).
--   6. Retires the hidden "Everything else" (status only, no forward).
--   7. Renames the 39 categories to their v2 labels and widens each one's
--      applicable_event_types to cover its services (never narrows).
--   8. Names every picker service and sets its applicable_event_types to v2's
--      hand-set list (v2 records −0 against live everywhere).
--   9. Writes every specialty as a pick-all-that-apply facet (Rental = yes/no),
--      with its question and each value's event scope (option_event_types,
--      inside the facet definition — no new column).
--  10. Tags every shop holding a folded key with that key's specialty value,
--      folding the key's own attribute row in first, then merges the trade.
--
-- NEVER merges a Setnayan product (pabati included) or hard-deletes a trade or
-- a category. IDEMPOTENT: a second run changes nothing. The run summary is
-- left in the session setting `setnayan.taxonomy_v2_2026_11_06`.

